            <ArticleTitle>Mobile dental clinic: an oral health care delivery model for underserved migrant children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>115-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate the oral health status, access, and the role of mobile dental clinics in improving the oral health of migrant children.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Parents attending University of Southern California's Mobile Dental Clinics completed a questionnaire about their children's access to dental care.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">54 percent of children were unable to access needed care, and prevalence of untreated decay was 87.4 percent.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Dental needs are high among migrant children. Mobile clinics provide a safety net for them.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
